    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is a derived, read-only attribute on the owner response \u2014 so I implemented it at the mapping edge rather than adding a persisted column or a new pipeline step.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the tier from the entity:\n   ```java\n   (owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()) ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\nSince `namesakeCount` (set by the existing `CountNamesakes` step) and `email` are both persisted at create time, the value is computed consistently on every `GET /api/owners/{id}` read. The two acceptance tests \u2014 `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique names + email \u2192 `SILVER`) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 `BRONZE`) \u2014 both pass.",
